# Component conventions

- Check `src/components/ui/` first. Reuse `Screen`, `Text`, `Button`, `Card` and
  `Badge` rather than rebuilding a plain `View` with utility classes.
- Never use React Native's `<Text>` directly. Use `@/components/ui/text`, which
  applies the type scale.
- Wrap every screen in `<Screen>` so safe-area insets and padding stay uniform.
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/cn` and accept a `className` prop so
  callers can override styling.
- Express variants as an object keyed by variant name, the way `button.tsx`
  does. Do not chain ternaries inside `className`.
- `src/components/ui/` holds generic, reusable pieces. Anything that knows about
  app data (a trip, a user) belongs in `src/components/`.
- Add `accessibilityRole` and `accessibilityLabel` to anything tappable.
- Handle three states for every list: loading, empty and populated.
